\section{Data Structures}

\subsection{LLM Decision}

An [[LLMDecision]] represents the LLM's classification of a single paper,
including its confidence score and reasoning.

<<llm review data structures>>=
@dataclass
class LLMDecision:
    """
    A single LLM classification decision for a paper.

    Attributes:
        paper_id: Identifier of the classified paper
        status: Classification result ("kept" or "discarded")
        tags: Themes (kept) or motivations (discarded) assigned
        confidence: LLM's confidence in the decision (0.0-1.0), or
            `None` when the answer gave none that is usable
        reasoning: Brief explanation of the classification
        dropped_tags: Tags the model proposed outside the vocabulary
        category_problem: Why the tags break the one-category rule
            (empty when they do not, or when the session has no
            category tags)
        answer_problem: Why the answer cannot be used as a decision
            (no answer, an invalid decision or confidence); empty when
            it can
        abstract_truncated: Whether the prompt showed only the start of
            the paper's abstract
    """
    paper_id: str
    status: str  # "kept" or "discarded"
    tags: list[str]
    confidence: float | None
    reasoning: str
    dropped_tags: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    category_problem: str = ""
    answer_problem: str = ""
    abstract_truncated: bool = False

    @property
    def problem(self) -> str:
        """Why the decision is withheld; empty when it is not."""
        return self.answer_problem or self.category_problem
@


