def _answer_index(value, count: int) -> int | None:
    """Return `value` as a paper index below `count`, or `None`."""
    if isinstance(value, str) and value.strip().isdigit():
        value = int(value)
    if isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, int):
        return None
    return value if 0 <= value < count else None
@

The parser used to repair every other defect with a default: a
decision it could not read became \enquote{kept} and a missing
confidence became 0.5.  Those values then looked exactly like the
model's own, in the session and in every report built from it, so a
report could state that the model kept a paper it had said nothing
sensible about.  Now a defect is recorded instead, in
[[answer_problem]], and the answer is withheld like one that breaks the
category rule (\cref{sec:classifier-categories}): the paper stays
pending, and [[scholar llm classify]] lists it at the end.  The
defects are a decision that is neither \enquote{kept} nor
\enquote{discarded}, a discard without any tag (which the review
module would hold invalid), and a confidence that is missing, not a
number, or outside $[0, 1]$.  An out-of-range confidence used to be
clamped, but a model that writes 85 probably means 85\,\%, and
clamping it to 1.0 would invent a certainty; we do not guess which
scale it used.

