@

A screened work can be in the session more than once, and every record
of it holds the verdict as surely as the screened one: a DOI-less copy
found by another provider, a preprint linked to the published version,
a second decision under the same id.  So a decision is hidden when it
shares any key of [[same_work_keys]] with a screened paper: its id, the
DOI of a version recorded on either record ([[version_link_dois]]), or
its title and first author's surname reduced as the audit table merges
rows ([[audit_work_key]], used only when the title keeps a letter or
digit, since every untitled record would share the empty key).  These
are the keys on which the sessions check relates records
([[session_match_index]] in the review module), without its guard
against namesakes ([[plausibly_same_work]]): here a namesake hidden
costs one example, while a copy shown would give the verdict away.

