<<llm review llm interaction>>=
def _check_one_category(
    tags: list[str], categories: set[str] | None
) -> tuple[list[str], str]:
    """Return `tags` with categories canonicalised, and what is wrong.

    The second element is empty when `tags` holds exactly one of
    `categories`, or when there are no categories to choose from.
    """
    if not categories:
        return tags, ""
    canonical = {c.casefold(): c for c in categories}
    checked: list[str] = []
    for tag in tags:
        tag = canonical.get(tag.casefold(), tag)
        if tag not in checked:
            checked.append(tag)
    found = [t for t in checked if t in categories]
    if len(found) == 1:
        return checked, ""
    if not found:
        return checked, "no category tag"
    return checked, "several category tags: " + ", ".join(found)
@

A paper that breaks the rule goes through the same single retry as a
paper left without tags, with the rule spelled out next to the
vocabulary. The retry's answer replaces the first one for the whole
batch, as it always has.

<<llm review llm interaction>>=
def _needs_retry(
    decisions: list[LLMDecision], allowed: set[str] | None
) -> bool:
    """Tell whether a paper lost all its tags or has no usable decision."""
    return any(
        (allowed and d.dropped_tags and not d.tags) or d.problem
        for d in decisions
    )


def _retry_reminder(
    allowed: set[str] | None, categories: set[str] | None
) -> str:
    """Spell out the vocabulary and the category rule for the retry."""
    lines = []
    if allowed:
        lines.append(
            "IMPORTANT: use only these tags, exactly as written: "
            + ", ".join(sorted(allowed))
        )
    if categories:
        ordered = sorted(categories, key=lambda t: AUDIT_CATEGORIES.get(t, 0))
        lines.append(
            "IMPORTANT: give every paper exactly one of these category "
            "tags: " + ", ".join(ordered)
            + "; any other tag is an optional extra. "
            + _category_status_rule(categories)
        )
    return "\n\n" + "\n".join(lines)
@

A paper that still has no single category after the retry gets no
decision at all. Recording it anyway would put a row into the audit
table under the wrong heading, or hide it from [[--bearing-only]],
which is the failure we set out to remove; left pending, it is counted
as unclassified in the caption and comes up again in the next batch or
for a human. The same holds for a paper whose answer is unusable
(\cref{sec:llm-parse}): it triggers the same single retry, for the
same reason as a paper left without tags (a second attempt costs less
than a paper a human has to classify), and if the retry does not mend
it the paper stays pending. The withheld decisions travel in the
batch result so that [[scholar llm classify]] can name them at the end
of the run.

