    ),
    "discarded": frozenset({"adjacent-subtopic", "off-topic-false-hit"}),
}
@

A contradicting answer is handled like one with no category or two:
it gets [[category_problem]], which triggers the single retry, and if
the retry does not mend it the paper is withheld and stays pending
(\cref{sec:classifier-categories}).  Withholding costs a human look at
one paper; recording it would cost an appendix row whose verdict
nobody made.  The check runs only once the paper has exactly one
category, so the message names the one problem the model can fix, and
only when the session has categories at all, like the rule it extends.

<<llm review llm interaction>>=
def _category_status_problem(
    status: str, tags: list[str], categories: set[str] | None
) -> str:
    """Return why the category in `tags` does not fit `status`, or "".

    `tags` holds exactly one of `categories`; `status` is "kept" or
    "discarded" (anything else is reported elsewhere).
    """
    if not categories or status not in STATUS_CATEGORIES:
        return ""
    category = next(t for t in tags if t in categories)
    if category in STATUS_CATEGORIES[status]:
        return ""
    return f"category {category} does not fit a {status} paper"
