A confirmation clears the flag.  On a decision that waits for review it
should be clear already: [[apply_llm_decisions]] and a machine
[[sessions decide]] both clear it, and [[sessions relabel]] moves it
into its record (\cref{sec:relabel-source} in the review module).  But
a file can hold one that is set, from a hand edit, an unknown source or
an older Scholar, and left set it would make the human's agreement read
as a change in every place that counts changes
([[machine_review_rows]], the CSV's [[llm_review_outcome]]).  The flag
means \enquote{a human changed the machine's verdict}, and after this
review that is exactly [[not user_agrees]].

