A plain sample with a size at least its population draws all of it, in
key order, as it always did, and is not marked as a census: its record
must not change.  A band of a stratified sample with at most [[size]]
members is taken whole and marked as a census, because the report
treats such a band differently: every member of it is (or will be)
reviewed, so its rate needs no interval.

<<draw the members with the smallest keys>>=
for stratum in strata:
    if census or (stratum.band is not None and len(stratum.pool) <= size):
        stratum.census = True
        stratum.drawn = list(stratum.pool)
        continue
    keys = [stratum.rng.random() for _ in stratum.pool]
    order = sorted(range(len(stratum.pool)), key=lambda i: (keys[i], i))
    stratum.drawn = [stratum.pool[i] for i in order[:size]]
@

Each stratum is recorded as an [[LLMSample]] with its own population,
digest and drawn papers.  A plain sample keeps exactly the criteria it
had before bounds from above existed; the new criteria are added only
when used, so a draw made as before stores what it stored before.
The bands of a stratified sample are tied together in their criteria
(\cref{sec:llm-sample-bands} says why there).

<<record the sample in each session>>=
drawn_at = (now or datetime.now(timezone.utc)).isoformat(timespec="seconds")
sample_id = (
    f"{drawn_at}/{'census' if seed is None else f'seed={seed}'}/"
    f"{uuid.uuid4().hex[:SAMPLE_ID_DIGITS]}"
)
sources = sorted({source_value(d) for s in strata for _, _, d in s.pool})
names = [session_label(s) for s in sessions]
files = [session_file_path(s).name for s in sessions]
for index, stratum in enumerate(strata):
