@

The id of a sample has to be unique, not only readable.  The time and
the seed alone are not enough: a [[--discarded]] and a [[--kept]] draw
started in the same second with the same seed would share an id, and
then [[sample_reports]] would add the kept rows to the discard rate and
the concurrent merge, which keeps one sample per id, would drop one of
them.  So the id ends in random hexadecimal digits from [[uuid4]].  The
id needs no reproducibility of its own: what makes the draw
reproducible is the seed, the criteria and the population, all of which
are stored beside it.

The draw is checked on three properties: the same seed over the same
population gives the same papers whatever order the sessions come in,
only eligible decisions are drawn, and each session records its own
share of the sample under one id:

