\paragraph{The other pooled sessions.}
\label{sec:llm-sample-report}
A report on one session of a sample pooled over several needs the
others too, read-only: [[llm sample --report]] and the report's LLM
screening section both read them with [[pooled_sample_sessions]].  A
sample names its sessions by label, which is not a key: the unnamed
session of query [[foo]] and a named session [[foo]] share the label,
and [[load_session]] opens [[foo.json]] first, so a sample pooled over
the unnamed session before a named [[foo]] was created counted the
named session's decisions, and its own sampled papers as not found
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/231}).  A sample
therefore keeps the file of each session ([[session_files]],
\cref{sec:llm-sample-record} in the review module), and the other
sessions are read from those files.  A file that is gone is a session
that no longer exists, and its papers are counted as not found; one
that cannot be read is skipped with the warning a listing gives
([[load_listed_session]]).  A sample drawn before the files were kept
has only the labels, which are looked up as before ([[load]], by
default [[load_session]]); then a session already read is not read
again, so a label that resolves to a given session's file adds nothing.
A recorded file is taken by its base name only: the field is read from
a session file that may have been edited by hand, and a name with a
directory part or [[..]] must not make the report read a file outside
the sessions directory.

<<llm review sampling>>=
def pooled_sample_sessions(
    sessions: list[ReviewSession],
    *,
    load: Callable[[str], ReviewSession | None] | None = None,
) -> list[ReviewSession]:
    """Return `sessions`, then the other sessions their samples pooled.

    The others are read from the files the samples record, or, for a
    sample drawn before files were recorded, looked up by label with
    `load` (default `load_session`). A session whose file is gone is
    left out, so its sampled papers count as not found.
    """
    import os

    from scholar.review import (
        _get_sessions_dir, load_listed_session, load_session,
        session_file_path,
    )

    load = load or load_session
    pooled = list(sessions)
    files = {session_file_path(s).name for s in sessions}
    labels = {session_label(s) for s in sessions}
    wanted_files: set[str] = set()
    wanted_labels: set[str] = set()
    for session in sessions:
        for sample in session.llm_samples:
            if sample.session_files is not None:
                wanted_files.update(
                    os.path.basename(f) for f in sample.session_files
                )
            else:
                wanted_labels.update(sample.sessions)
    for file_name in sorted(wanted_files - files):
        path = _get_sessions_dir() / file_name
        other = load_listed_session({"path": path}) if path.exists() else None
        if other is not None:
            pooled.append(other)
            files.add(file_name)
    for label in sorted(wanted_labels - labels):
        other = load(label)
        if other is not None and session_file_path(other).name not in files:
            pooled.append(other)
            files.add(session_file_path(other).name)
    return pooled
@

The TUI queues a sample for review through [[sampled_for_review]]:
the session's sampled decisions that still wait for a human, in the
order they were drawn, each once even when two samples drew it.  A
paper reset since a sample's draw is not queued for that sample: its
new call was never drawn.

<<llm review sampling>>=
def sampled_for_review(session: ReviewSession) -> list[ReviewDecision]:
    """Return the sampled decisions of `session` not yet reviewed."""
    from scholar.notes import get_paper_id

    current = {get_paper_id(d.paper): d for d in session.decisions}
    queue: list[ReviewDecision] = []
    queued: set[str] = set()
    for sample in session.llm_samples:
        for entry in sample.papers:
            decision = current.get(entry["paper_id"])
            if (
                decision is not None
                and is_unreviewed_machine(decision)
                and not reset_since_draw(decision, sample.drawn_at)
                and entry["paper_id"] not in queued
            ):
                queue.append(decision)
                queued.add(entry["paper_id"])
    return queue
@

