The reasons for withholding the estimate are checked in an order that
names the first thing the user can act on.  A band record missing from
the sessions comes first, since nothing else can be judged without it.
Decisions not found come next: a pooled session whose file is gone, or
one not given to the report, takes a whole session's share of every
band, and the bands' rates would then be one session's rates
extrapolated to all, a loss that has everything to do with which
decisions were lost.  Then decisions still waiting for a review, and
last a band whose every drawn decision was reset since the draw, which
has no review left to estimate its rate from; it is named, since
nothing is waiting in it and the user would otherwise not see why.

