\subsection{The screening paragraphs of the report}

The review report describes the LLM step through
[[build_llm_screening_latex]], which the report calls in one line
(\cref{sec:report-llm-screening} in the review module).  It states how
many decisions an LLM made, with the models, the prompt versions and
the dates the decisions record, how many of them saw a truncated
abstract, and for how many none of this was recorded; then one
sentence per sample stored in the session, one for all the bands of a
stratified sample (\cref{sec:llm-sample-stratified-report}).  A session
without LLM decisions and without samples gets nothing, so the report
never describes a step that did not happen.  The truncation is stated from
each decision's own [[llm_abstract_truncated]], without a number of
characters: the limit is today's [[MAX_ABSTRACT_CHARS]], but a decision
made under an earlier limit was cut at that one, and only its prompt
version records which.

A sample pooled over several sessions is reported over all of them:
the function loads the other sessions it names, read-only, through
[[load]] (by default the review module's [[load_session]]), and a
session it cannot load is counted under \enquote{not found} by
[[sample_reports]].

A decision was first made by an LLM when its source says so, but not
only then.  [[sessions relabel]] turns an LLM call that an agent
confirmed into an [[agent]] decision and keeps the classifier's fields
(\cref{sec:relabel-source} in the review module); counting sources
alone dropped those rows from the sentence, and their model and prompt
from the report.  So a
decision also counts when it holds the classifier's model, which only
[[apply_llm_decisions]] writes and a machine [[sessions decide]]
clears unless given [[--keep-trace]], or when one of its relabel
records says it came from an LLM source.  With [[--keep-trace]]
(\cref{sec:sessions-decide} in the CLI module), an agent's correction
of a classifier call still counts here, with the call's model and
prompt.

A pending paper never counts, whatever its history.  The sentence
counts decisions, and a paper set back to pending ([[sessions reset]],
\cref{sec:reset-decision} in the review module) has none: its old
call is kept in its reset history, not in the fields the report reads,
but its relabel records stay, and one that says \enquote{from llm}
would otherwise count a paper nobody has decided.  Once [[llm
classify]] decides it again, it counts by its new source and model.

