The prompt holds no verdict of a screened paper: neither its tags nor
its reasons, its title appears once, among the papers to classify, and
that part of the prompt has no status or category word.  The strongest
form of the check: with the screened papers' verdicts turned round,
the prompt is the same, byte for byte.  The other decided papers
still serve as examples, with their tags; and a batch of every decided
paper, which leaves no example and no tag of the session's, is still
offered the categories.

