\subsubsection{Keys for the appendix}
\label{sec:synthesis-key-space}

The \LaTeX{} synthesis ends with the decision record, which
[[\fullcite]]s every paper the review touched, so the bibliography must
hold keys for the discarded papers and for kept papers that
[[--max-papers]] left out of the prose. Those keys join the same key
space as the cited papers, and that space must be extended without
disturbing what is already there: theme sections are cached under
[[_theme_cache_key]], which hashes paper fingerprints but not the keys,
and the cached prose contains the keys literally. The extension is safe
because collision suffixes are assigned in iteration order---appending
papers can suffix later entries, never earlier ones---provided the
included kept papers come first, in their original order.

The space is deduplicated by paper id. A session can hold the same paper
twice (the loader derives arXiv DOIs from URLs, so two records saved as
distinct can coincide on reload), and two entries under one key make
biber abort; keeping the first occurrence resolves both citations to it.

<<llm review synthesis>>=
def _unique_by_paper_id(
    decisions: list[ReviewDecision],
) -> list[ReviewDecision]:
    """Drop later decisions whose paper id was already seen."""
    from scholar.notes import get_paper_id

    unique: list[ReviewDecision] = []
    seen: set[str] = set()
    for decision in decisions:
        paper_id = get_paper_id(decision.paper)
        if paper_id in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(paper_id)
        unique.append(decision)
    return unique


def _synthesis_key_space(
    session: ReviewSession,
    kept_decisions: list[ReviewDecision],
) -> list[ReviewDecision]:
    """Order all decisions so the keys of `kept_decisions` never change.

    The included kept papers come first in their original order, then
    the remaining kept papers, then the discarded ones; duplicates by
    paper id are dropped.
    """
    return _unique_by_paper_id(
        list(kept_decisions)
        + session.kept_papers()
        + session.discarded_papers()
    )
@

