The provenance section's summary counts the decisions by source, as the
review report does (\cref{sec:review-source}): a synthesis built on
papers an agent or a model kept without a human reading them must say
so where it gives the numbers (issue~\#163).  The rows come from
[[decision_source_rows]], so the synthesis and the report use the same
wording, including the note on how many decisions of a source that
claims a human carry a record of the review, when any lacks one, and
the sentence after the summary that explains it
(\cref{sec:human-review-record} in the review module).

